# W2b — DeepGEMM E8M0 scales off.
# VERDICT 2026-09-03: FAILED (correctness), never re-run. The stack boots (rank-0 log:
# "DeepGEMM E8M0 disabled on current configuration", Triton MoE, an extra ~6 min DeepGEMM
# warmup of 1133 shapes before weight loading) but generates degenerate text: a chat
# request answers "lockhandlehandlehandle..." (temperature 0, thinking off); decode prose
# 14.6 tok/s [13.5-18.2] and prefill 30k 2309 tok/s are meaningless on garbage output.
# The patched DeepGEMM on sm121 needs the UE8M0 scale path; float scales are unsupported.
# With VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM_E8M0=0 the MoE dispatch follows _valid_deep_gemm(): for this
# model N=512 per rank at TP4, so "N <= 512" sends every shape to the Triton fused MoE,
# and the dense FP8 linears drop the UE8M0 requantization (boot-and-see on sm121: the
# patched DeepGEMM may or may not accept float scales; a boot abort shows within 10 min,
# then fall back to W2a). Rollback: ./tp4ctl restart without TP4_ENV (~22 min).
EXTRA_DOCKER_ENV="-e VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM_E8M0=0"
